cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Structural joints and aerodynamic fairings for a blood-transport UAV: design,
  manufacture and test
message: If you refer to this work, please cite it using these metadata.
type: dataset
authors:
  - given-names: Jad
    family-names: El Badaoui
    affiliation: University of Bristol
abstract: >-
  Design, analysis, manufacture and testing of the joints and fairings subassembly
  for a blood-transport UAV, delivered as part of the AVDASI 2 group design project
  at the University of Bristol. Ten additively manufactured flight parts totalling
  1,011 g, taken from requirements and concept downselection through stress analysis
  and reserve factors to a wind tunnel entry and a load test past the ultimate load
  case. The airframe survived to 813 N with a linear load-deflection response, but
  failed by bolt shear-out through a 3D-printed clamp -- a path for which no reserve
  factor had been computed, which is the most useful engineering finding in the work.
  Documented from the author's own vantage point, with contribution scoped explicitly
  and teammates referred to by role.
keywords:
  - unmanned aerial vehicle
  - aerospace structures
  - structural analysis
  - reserve factor
  - additive manufacturing
  - wind tunnel testing
  - computer-aided design
  - aerodynamics
  - engineering design
  - project management
